{
  "title": "Composing Global Solutions to Reasoning Tasks via Algebraic Objects in Neural Nets",
  "authors": [
    "Yuandong Tian"
  ],
  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2410.01779",
  "abstract": "This paper introduces a framework called CoGS, which enables the construction of global optimal solutions for 2-layer neural networks with quadratic activation and L2 loss, trained on reasoning tasks in Abelian groups. The framework is based on the discovery of rich algebraic structures of the solution space, allowing for the composition of partial solutions into global ones using ring operations.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "The paper explores how to compose global solutions to reasoning tasks, such as modular addition, using algebraic objects in neural networks. The key insight is that the solution space of 2-layer neural networks with quadratic activation and L2 loss has a rich algebraic structure, enabling the composition of partial solutions into global ones.",
